{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"halfalive-unexisting-sow","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Mechanism: ChatGPT.app codex (single long-lived process) launches a fresh MCP server stack (uvx serena start-mcp-server --context codex + pyright-langserver + node + headroom mcp wrapper) per conversation epoch and leaves prior stacks running when conversations end. Stale stacks (~1.2GB each, observed 4 epochs Sep 6/7/9/10 under codex PID 11153) go fully swapped-out and stop draining their FSEventStreams while remaining registered clients. Under rebar's fs-event volume (~19.2k-test runs, worktree churn) fseventsd accretes per-client/event buffers without bound and never returns memory (peak==current): reached 107GB phys_footprint by day 4 of the Sep 6 boot, nearly exhausting 128GB RAM + 68GB swap — recurrence of incident 2ab6-bae5-8ca4-429c (whose open follow-up flagged exactly this uv->python blocked-pair leak). Claude/Copilot ide-assistant serena instances do NOT accumulate (parents reap them). Mitigation applied 2026-09-10: serena disabled for codex (~/.codex/config.toml enabled=false, annotated); stale stacks killed by pid; fseventsd restarted by operator. Acceptance criteria: (1) decide + document the sanctioned codex/serena configuration (keep disabled, or re-enable only with a reaping/idle-exit mechanism, e.g. serena idle timeout or a codex upgrade that terminates MCP servers on conversation end); (2) add fseventsd footprint to the mem-sentinel launchd snapshots so accretion is alarmed before jetsam; (3) verify after one week of normal agent load that fseventsd stays <5GB. Evidence: .rebar/scratch/memleak-copilot-87759/ and comments on 2ab6-bae5-8ca4-429c.","id":"4e15-14a6-e60d-4e90","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Codex spawns one serena/pyright MCP stack per conversation and never reaps old ones — stale FSEvents clients drive fseventsd accretion (2026-09-10 near-exhaustion recurrence)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789059308119608001,"uuid":"94767e62-3a7b-4363-b440-7fbd385e8830"}